  "solution": {
    "text": "Reactions take place at electrodes are <br/>At cathode <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>  <br/>At cathode <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>→</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>  <br/>For the deposition of 197 g (1 mole) of Au = 3F of charge is required thus, for the deposition of 78 g of Au, charge required <br/><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>197</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>78</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1.19</mn><mtext>F</mtext></math>  <br/><math><mo>=</mo><mn>1.19</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>96500</mn></math> coulumbs <br/>From <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math>  <br/><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.19</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>96500</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>  <br/><math><mo>=</mo><mn>19139.16</mn></math> sec <br/>By 1 F charge, 35.5 g of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> gas is formed, thus from 1.19 F, mass of chlorine gas formed <math><mo>=</mo><mn>35.5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1.19</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>42.24</mn></math> g"
